ents{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"closed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2016-04-10T22:37:46Z","state_reason":null,"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/issues/comments/208086499","html_url":"https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/issues/120#issuecomment-208086499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/issues/120","id":208086499,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIwODA4NjQ5OQ==","user":{"login":"brian-mann","id":1268976,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjg5NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1268976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-mann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-04-10T22:41:25Z","updated_at":"2016-04-10T22:41:25Z","body":"Open a new issue for passing a dir to `--spec` since that is a new feature, and we'll track it better that way.\n\nAs for passing `--spec` to `cypress ci` that's going to be a no go. I understand why you want to do it since you're essentially using `cypress ci` as an alternate to `cypress run` due to not being able to log in from the command line.\n\nAt the moment there's not much difference between `cypress ci` and `cypress run` but soon they will be two very different things. One will spin up real browser instances, record the screen, take screenshots, do analysis, and make the build results available to you, which will take up build hours. The other will simply run the tests locally and will not record any permanent results.\n\nThis platform will be rolling out fairly soon and if we just added the ability to log in from the command line then my guess is you'd use `cypress run`.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/issues/comments/208086499/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"brian-mann","id":1268976,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjg5NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1268976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann","html_url":"https://github.com/brian-mann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brian-mann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2009087971,"node_id":"MDExOkxvY2tlZEV2ZW50MjAwOTA4Nzk3MQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cypress-io/cypress/issues/events/2009087971","actor":{"login":"cypress-io","id":8908513,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2